# Telegram sign-in for registration. The token signs the payload the widget
# hands the browser, and the server re-derives that signature before it will
# create an account, so this value is the whole basis for trusting an identity.
# It is never sent to the browser; only TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME is.
#
# Both keys come from @BotFather. Keep this file out of git.
#
# TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=1234567890:replace-with-the-real-token
# TELEGRAM_BOT_USERNAME=your_bot_without_the_at_sign
